{
  "id": "80856",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Equilibrium Constant Calculations",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Previously, we discussed the law of mass action, the equilibrium constant expression, and how to use equilibrium concentrations to determine the value of the equilibrium constant. For example, if for the reversible reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "wv1yvicjykop1ne",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "maaq8qdxs87ozvy",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "gi6t6l5gt1wqv3z",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm{NH}}_3(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm N}_2(g)\\;+\\;3\\;{\\mathrm H}_2(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "the equilibrium concentrations are [N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] = 0.58 M, [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] = 0.75 M, and [NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "] = 0.35 M at 400 °C, we can calculate "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "c"
              },
              {
                "text": " at this temperature."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ibsfkxfmhcrdcxi",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "6rjjn72e7zykqzo",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1p0ocs5v8iavwf7",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "K_\\mathrm{c}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\left[{\\mathrm N}_2\\right]\\left[{\\mathrm H}_2\\right]^3}{\\left[{\\mathrm{NH}}_3\\right]^2}\\; =\\;\\frac{(0.58)(0.75)^3}{(0.35)^2}\\;=\\;2.0",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Likewise, given "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "c"
              },
              {
                "text": " and all but one equilibrium concentration, this unknown equilibrium concentration can be calculated using the equilibrium constant expression, as we see in the following example."
              }
            ],
            "id": "qbjmojjuiul36yt",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "402993919",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Nitrogen oxides are air pollutants produced by the reaction of nitrogen and oxygen at high temperatures. For the reaction:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "u5xnzz70e97ya17",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "j4knjo4vtz8jxzs",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4wmpo3fxsn1kkzq",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm N}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm O}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{NO}(g)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "the value of the equilibrium constant "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "c"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is 4.1 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at 2000 °C. Find the concentration of NO("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "g"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") in an equilibrium mixture with air at 1 atm pressure at this temperature. In air, [N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.036 M and [O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.0089 M."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "9u4ves3xtoqlug4",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We are given all of the equilibrium concentrations except for NO. Thus, we can solve for the missing equilibrium concentration by rearranging the equilibrium constant equation:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "h308b6rjjqmp1b3",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "bvxqg5upbme1a03",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a5dlkynammtxrir",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_\\mathrm{c}=\\frac{\\left[\\mathrm{NO}\\right]^2}{\\left[{\\mathrm N}_2\\right]\\left[{\\mathrm O}_2\\right]}\\;\\;\\;\\; \\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;\\left[\\mathrm{NO}\\right]^2=K_\\mathrm{c}\\;\\left[{\\mathrm N}_2\\right]\\left[{\\mathrm O}_2\\right]",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "m1300dyv3kqi4ub",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "s4ytlfahv3czwbl",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\left[\\mathrm{NO}\\right]=\\sqrt{K_\\mathrm{c}\\;\\left[{\\mathrm N}_2\\right]\\left[{\\mathrm O}_2\\right]}=\\sqrt{\\left(4.1\\times10^{-4} \\right)\\left(0.036\\right)\\left(0.0089\\right)}=3.6\\times10^{-4}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Thus, [NO] is 3.6 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M at equilibrium under these conditions."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "k5e49fap4q8i75t",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We can check our answer by substituting all equilibrium concentrations into the equilibrium constant expression:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "6irkc653j73jpr0",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "u512sfm6q4yb0e5",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "l1873gtxx2dqvwi",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_\\mathrm{c}=\\frac{\\left[\\mathrm{NO}\\right]^2}{\\left[{\\mathrm N}_2\\right]\\left[{\\mathrm O}_2\\right]}=\\frac{\\left(3.6\\times10^{-4} \\right)^2}{\\left(0.036\\right)\\left(0.0089\\right)}=4.1\\times10^{-4}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The answer checks. Our calculated value gives the equilibrium constant within the error associated with the significant figures in the problem."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1ix2v0jl4z61ouc",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "3521882081",
